DOCKLINER_PORT=54542
# DOCKLINER_SERVICE=dockliner
# Database
DOCKLINER_DB_TYPE=sqlite
DOCKLINER_DB_PATH=./dockliner.db


in dockliner we need the db setup in a way i say, also the port things

1. we need the DB_MODE set to either auto or test or live, if auto it will resolve itself autometicly, but if live/test it will ask for DB_LIVE_ initialization variables
    and actually we can have DB_TYPE too to specify the type of database to use (sqlite, postgres, mysql, etc.).
    The options for DB_MODE are:
        . auto = automatically choose the database according to found environment variables
        . test = use a test database (for development/testing purposes) mostly sqlite and no need to be specify even
        . live = use a live database (for production purposes) mostly postgres or mysql, strictly need to be specified with the DB_LIVE_ initialization variables
    And the options for DB_TYPE are:
        . sqlite = use SQLite database
        . postgres = use PostgreSQL database
        . mysql = use MySQL database
    the live or test will only make difference in the initialization of the database, migrations and without setup auto availablity

    after that we need like DB_LIVE_HOST, DB_LIVE_PORT, DB_LIVE_USER, DB_LIVE_PASSWORD, DB_LIVE_NAME and even SQLITE_DB_PATH SQLITE_DB_NAME
    and in case of test database same can be set,


2. we need the port to be configurable through environment variables, allowing users to specify the desired port for the application to run on. If no port is occupied return error and turn off the application imidiately, but if the port is not configured but user ran a command to setup the application like by sh or ps1
   script, then it should automatically choose a free port and inform the user about the chosen port.

and most importantly, we need to have command and script to setup the application on any environment, but also detecting the port issue on initial stage, and reserve port will be from 50000+ but any prime number port should get not none-prime number port

also need local-database deleting system like i can delete sqlite after setting up the live database, and also a command to switch between test and live database modes, with proper migration handling. (i think env can do properly)

